{"schema_version":"1.0.0","document_id":"61ca3b5f7935b6dde56f5330320c86763f6782ec33c38f9a3da636b0d9465b2d","company_key":"capitol-federal-financial-inc-common-stock","company_name":"Capitol Federal Financial Inc.","source_id":"capitol-federal-financial-inc-common-stock-news-import-d06bee8b7ae1","source_kind":"html","canonical_url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/capitol-federal-financial-inc-announces-quarterly-dividend-163162426.html","observed_url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/capitol-federal-financial-inc-announces-quarterly-dividend-163162426.html","title":"Capitol Federal Financial, Inc. Announces Quarterly Dividend","summary":"/PRNewswire/ -- Capitol Federal Financial, Inc. (Nasdaq: CFFN) (the \"Company\") announced today that its Board of Directors has declared a quarterly cash...","body_text":"TOPEKA, Kan. , July 20, 2012 /PRNewswire/ -- Capitol Federal Financial, Inc. (Nasdaq: CFFN ) (the \"Company\") announced today that its Board of Directors has declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.075 per share on outstanding CFFN common stock. The dividend is payable on August 17, 2012 to stockholders of record as of the close of business on August 3, 2012 . CFFN will announce financial results for the quarter ended June 30, 2012 on July 30 , 2012. The Company's Form 10-Q will be filed on or about August 3, 2012 . Capitol Federal Financial, Inc. is the holding company for Capitol Federal Savings Bank, which operates 45 branch offices in Kansas and Missouri. News and other information about the Company can be found on the Bank's website, www.capfed.com . Except for the historical information contained in this press release, the matters discussed may be deemed to be forward-looking statements, within the meaning of the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995, that involve risks and uncertainties, including changes in economic conditions in the Company's market are, changes in policies by regulatory agencies and other governmental initiatives affecting the financial services industry, fluctuations in interest rates, demand for loans in the Company's market are, the future earnings and capital levels of Capitol Federal Savings Bank, which could affect the ability of the Company to pay dividends in accordance with its dividend policies, competition, and other risks detailed from time to time in the Company's SEC reports. Actual results in future periods may differ materially from those currently expected. These forward-looking statements represent the Company's judgment as of the date of this release. The Company disclaims, however, any intent or obligation to update these forward-looking statements. SOURCE Capitol Federal Financial","published_at":"2012-07-20T12:30:00+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-07-24T23:25:18.049976+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-07-28T21:33:52.463534+00:00","last_updated_at":"2026-08-19T21:01:48.044486+00:00","content_hash":"sha256:bb52f34aaa660a77b4b91f51ec76b52d5bb9222a49c5c53e600d0624b133053b","article_path":"articles/v1/f3/capitol-federal-financial-inc-common-stock/2012/07/61/61ca3b5f7935b6dde56f5330320c86763f6782ec33c38f9a3da636b0d9465b2d/article.md","record_path":"articles/v1/f3/capitol-federal-financial-inc-common-stock/2012/07/61/61ca3b5f7935b6dde56f5330320c86763f6782ec33c38f9a3da636b0d9465b2d/record.json"}
{"schema_version":"1.0.0","document_id":"c99dbde777317fa078a1b5117807583cccd6e435e750be88775fe93db2afae14","company_key":"ironwood-pharmaceuticals-inc-class-a-common-stock","company_name":"Ironwood Pharmaceuticals Inc.","source_id":"ironwood-pharmaceuticals-inc-class-a-common-stock-rss-0257ece950a4","source_kind":"rss","canonical_url":"https://investor.ironwoodpharma.com/press-releases/press-release-details/2012/Ironwood-Pharmaceuticals-to-Host-Second-Quarter-2012-Investor-Update-Call/default.aspx","observed_url":"https://investor.ironwoodpharma.com/press-releases/press-release-details/2012/Ironwood-Pharmaceuticals-to-Host-Second-Quarter-2012-Investor-Update-Call/default.aspx","title":"Ironwood Pharmaceuticals to Host Second Quarter 2012 Investor Update Call","summary":"","body_text":"","published_at":"2012-07-10T04:00:00+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-08-18T10:31:29.990145+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-08-19T17:42:13.567804+00:00","last_updated_at":"2026-08-19T17:42:14.007354+00:00","content_hash":"sha256:f0dd7723c3b584ca4ac7aeca10192cfc52e76cd78ca2cd0bfe9de79dbb0e0faf","article_path":"articles/v1/a5/ironwood-pharmaceuticals-inc-class-a-common-stock/2012/07/c9/c99dbde777317fa078a1b5117807583cccd6e435e750be88775fe93db2afae14/article.md","record_path":"articles/v1/a5/ironwood-pharmaceuticals-inc-class-a-common-stock/2012/07/c9/c99dbde777317fa078a1b5117807583cccd6e435e750be88775fe93db2afae14/record.json"}
{"schema_version":"1.0.0","document_id":"f21cca0335452c70158d11d963299673c5187160d16f13bb975fa2720661279f","company_key":"yc-acunote","company_name":"Acunote","source_id":"yc-acunote-news-import-fc65b5e5f495","source_kind":"html","canonical_url":"https://www.acunote.com/blog/2012/07/why-we-did-y-combinator-acunote-yc-w11.html","observed_url":"https://www.acunote.com/blog/2012/07/why-we-did-y-combinator-acunote-yc-w11.html","title":"Why We Did YC - Acunote (YC W11)","summary":"","body_text":"Today Acunote officially launched as a Y Combinator company. Thanks Ingrid/TC, great article! That's exciting for us and our customers, and we'll have more fun stuff to report on this in the weeks and months ahead. But this post is not only about that. It's about a question that people always ask me - \"Why did you go into YC?\" Or what they really mean - \"Why would a profitable business go into YC?\" Acunote launches w/ YC, we wear silly hats We went into YC as a successful small business because we saw an opportunity to turn it into a huge business. This is a hard thing to do. Looking back at it the biggest thing YC gave us is alumni network . And this goes beyond access and advice. Being around YC alumni sets your expectations higher. It redefines the normal. If you want to do hard things - nothing helps more than believing that getting hard things done is normal. Another non-obvious benefit is that it gives you a large network of companies you trust implicitly. As Tony Soprano said \"It's hard doing business with strangers.\" YC companies are no strangers, same batch or not. It's easy to focus on value of YC brand and advice from the partners. And these are super - no doubt. But the real gold is in the network .","published_at":"2012-07-02T00:00:00+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-07-24T14:19:11.091402+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-07-28T21:33:52.463534+00:00","last_updated_at":"2026-08-19T20:44:00.912299+00:00","content_hash":"sha256:6aadca9ae29148e1844f9d193314d8c098254d12ac628df0d261b7ed72c90551","article_path":"articles/v1/6d/yc-acunote/2012/07/f2/f21cca0335452c70158d11d963299673c5187160d16f13bb975fa2720661279f/article.md","record_path":"articles/v1/6d/yc-acunote/2012/07/f2/f21cca0335452c70158d11d963299673c5187160d16f13bb975fa2720661279f/record.json"}
